  "foodhistory-timeline-baseline-milling": 'For most of history, flour kept its fiber and B vitamins. The steel roller mill stripped them out within one generation.',
  "foodhistory-timeline-chemical-convenience": 'From 1945 to 1976, DDT, new farm chemicals and margarine all spread. Those were the same years IBD first became common in industrial nations.',
  "foodhistory-timeline-glyphosate-hfcs": 'In the 1970s and 1980s, two new things entered our food: the weed killer glyphosate and corn syrup high in fructose.',
  "foodhistory-scapegoat-salt": 'Salt is tied to blood pressure, but about 70% of the sodium people eat comes from packaged food, not the salt shaker. Very low and very high salt both went with more deaths in one large analysis.',
