  "foodhistory-scapegoat-pattern": 'The same story keeps coming back. A whole food takes the blame, and the factory swap gets a pass. Sometimes the swap was worse.',
  "foodhistory-cholesterol-real-drivers": 'Genes are the strongest cause of very high cholesterol for about 1 in 200 people. For everyone else, how much saturated fat matters is still argued.',
  "foodhistory-apob-particle-count": 'A test called apoB counts the harmful particles that carry cholesterol. In a study across 52 countries, it told heart attack risk better than LDL.',
  "foodhistory-eggs-nutrient-density": 'Eggs are not just free of the harm they were blamed for. They pack protein, choline and many vitamins into a small food.',
  "foodhistory-butter-short-chain-fat": 'Butter has butyrate, a short fat the body handles in a different way than other fats. Its gut benefits were shown mostly in animals.',
  "foodhistory-mechanism-disappearing-microbiota": 'One idea says that over many years, antibiotics, C-sections and formula have cut the germs in our guts. It is an idea, not a proven fact.',
  "foodhistory-opinion-synthesis": 'This entry is the opinion of Claude, the AI that helped build the app, about the food history story. It is not proof, and more diagnosis explains part of the rise in disease.',
  "advocacy-why-it-matters": 'A normal checkup is short and covers the basics. A fuller set of lab tests usually has to be asked for by name.',
  "advocacy-magnesium": 'A magnesium blood test is worth asking for, but it sees less than 1% of the magnesium in your body. A normal result does not rule out low levels.',
  "advocacy-zinc-copper": 'Ask for zinc and copper to be tested together, above all if you take zinc. Too much zinc can cause low copper, which has led to anemia and nerve damage.',
  "advocacy-cbc": 'One blood test, the CBC, can catch anemia from low iron or low B12, a hidden infection and more.',
  "advocacy-fasting-insulin": 'Fasting insulin may rise years before blood sugar does. How well it predicts diabetes on its own is still debated.',
  "advocacy-hscrp": 'Hs-CRP is a blood test for inflammation you can track. It is useful now and then, not something to chase every month.',
  "advocacy-sex-hormones-menopause": 'Hormone tests can be useful, but they are often not needed to confirm perimenopause. Symptoms and age usually tell more.',
  "advocacy-how-to-ask": 'Bring a written list of the tests and questions you want to raise. People who do get more of their questions answered.',
  "advocacy-prescribing-cascade": "Sometimes a drug's side effect is taken for a new problem and treated with a second drug. This is called a prescribing cascade, and any change to your medicines is your doctor's call.",
  "handson-three-therapies-compared": 'Chiropractic, acupuncture and deep massage often get lumped together. The proof behind each one is not alike at all.',
